      "content": "It can be incredibly difficult to feel like you're not just going through the motions, but that your very sense of self has been lost. It's as if you've been asked to carry on without a foundation, leaving you feeling ungrounded and adrift. It may take time, but small, incremental changes to your daily routine and interests can sometimes help you uncover a glimmer of what's left of your identity, even if it's fragile. Allow yourself to feel the pain of losing the aspect of yourself that was tied to this other person, but try to hold onto the hope that you can find a way to rebuild and rediscover your own sense of self.",
