      "content": "but what if there's nothing to rebuild? u keep talking about finding a \"glimmer\" or \"rebuilding,\" but it's like trying to build a house on top of a void. it just feels heavy. like, why bother trying to fix something that was never actually there on its own? it feels more logical to just accept that the person i was is gone for good. it feels like i'm just performing a role for an audience that isn't even watching anymore.",
